---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { destinations, skiStatus, SKI_LABEL, SKI_RATING, MONTH_SHORT, MONTH_SLUGS, deg } from '../../lib/data';

const skiers = destinations.filter((d) => d.ski);
const regions: { label: string; slugs: string[] }[] = [
  { label: 'The Alps', slugs: ['switzerland', 'innsbruck', 'chamonix', 'dolomites'] },
  { label: 'North America', slugs: ['whistler', 'banff', 'colorado', 'park-city', 'lake-tahoe', 'grand-teton', 'vermont'] },
  { label: 'Japan & the Arctic', slugs: ['hokkaido', 'lapland'] },
  { label: 'Southern hemisphere', slugs: ['queenstown', 'santiago-chile', 'bariloche'] },
];
const rows = regions.map((r) => ({ ...r, items: r.slugs.map((s) => skiers.find((d) => d.slug === s)).filter((d) => d !== undefined) }));
const SHORT: Record<string, string> = { peak: 'Peak', season: 'Open', early: 'Opening', late: 'Late', glacier: 'Glacier' };
---

<Guide slug="ski-season" photo="dolomites">
  <p>
    In the northern hemisphere, the main ski season runs from <strong>December to April</strong>, with the most reliable snow
    from <strong>mid-January to mid-March</strong>. In the southern hemisphere — New Zealand, Chile and Argentina — it runs
    from about <strong>late June to late September</strong>. Add glacier skiing in the Alps and a handful of very high or very
    snowy resorts, and you can ski somewhere in every month of the year.
  </p>
  <p>
    Opening and closing dates depend on snowfall and change every year, so treat this calendar as a guide and check resort
    websites and snow reports before you book.
  </p>

  <h2>Ski season calendar</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="data-table ski">
      <caption class="visually-hidden">Ski season by destination and month</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Destination</th>{MONTH_SHORT.map((m) => <th scope="col">{m}</th>)}</tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          rows.flatMap((r) => [
            <tr class="group"><th scope="rowgroup" colspan="13">{r.label}</th></tr>,
            ...r.items.map((d) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row"><a href={d.url}>{d.name}</a></th>
                {MONTH_SHORT.map((_, m) => {
                  const s = skiStatus(d, m);
                  return <td>{s ? <span class="badge" data-rating={SKI_RATING[s]} title={SKI_LABEL[s]}>{SHORT[s]}</span> : <span class="muted">—</span>}</td>;
                })}
              </tr>
            )),
          ])
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">
    Peak = the most reliable snow and terrain; Open = main season; Opening/Late = early- or late-season conditions;
    Glacier = limited summer skiing on high glaciers. Month by month: {MONTH_SLUGS.map((s, m) => <><a href={`/where-to-ski-in-${s}/`}>{MONTH_SHORT[m]}</a>{m < 11 ? ' · ' : ''}</>)}
  </p>

  <h2>The Alps: December to April</h2>
  <p>
    Most Alpine resorts open in early-to-mid December and close after Easter. January brings cold, quiet slopes; February
    is the snowiest and busiest month thanks to school holidays across Europe; and March offers deep bases, longer days and
    sunny spring skiing. High resorts such as Zermatt, Val Thorens and those around Innsbruck are the safest bets early and
    late in the season, and glaciers like the <b>Hintertux Glacier</b> (open all year) and <b>Zermatt’s Matterhorn Glacier
    Paradise</b> offer summer skiing on a few high runs.
  </p>

  <h2>North America: November to April</h2>
  <p>
    Colorado’s highest resorts often open in late October, and most of the Rockies, Utah, Lake Tahoe and Whistler are running
    by Thanksgiving or early December. <b>January to March</b> is prime time: Utah and Whistler are famous for big snowfall,
    Colorado for dry powder and sunshine. Spring skiing lasts into April almost everywhere, into May at Whistler, Sunshine
    Village and Palisades Tahoe, and sometimes into June at Colorado’s Arapahoe Basin.
  </p>

  <h2>Japan: December to April, powder in January and February</h2>
  <p>
    Cold Siberian air picks up moisture over the Sea of Japan and drops it as light, dry snow on <a href="/destinations/hokkaido/">Hokkaido</a>
    and the Japan Alps. <b>Mid-January to mid-February</b> is the heart of ‘Japow’ season in Niseko, Rusutsu and Furano. December
    can be hit-and-miss early on; March brings sunnier, softer spring snow.
  </p>

  <h2>The southern hemisphere: late June to September</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/destinations/queenstown/">Queenstown’s</a> resorts — Coronet Peak, The Remarkables and Cardrona — usually open in
    mid-June and run into early October, with the best conditions in July and August. In South America, resorts near{' '}
    <a href="/destinations/santiago-chile/">Santiago</a> (Valle Nevado, La Parva, Portillo) and{' '}
    <a href="/destinations/bariloche/">Bariloche</a> (Cerro Catedral) run from late June to September. July coincides with local
    school holidays, so August is often quieter.
  </p>

  <h2>Tips for planning a ski trip</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Avoid school holidays</b> if you can: Christmas–New Year, mid-February half-term in Europe, and Presidents’ Day weekend in the US are the busiest and most expensive weeks.</li>
    <li><b>Go high early and late.</b> In December and April, pick resorts with high-altitude terrain or glaciers for more reliable snow.</li>
    <li><b>Look at multi-resort passes.</b> Season passes such as Epic and Ikon can pay for themselves in a week at the big North American resorts — buy them in spring or autumn before prices rise.</li>
    <li><b>Book lessons and rentals in advance</b> for peak weeks, and buy travel insurance that covers winter sports.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The town temperatures we show on destination pages are measured in the valley; the slopes are much colder — in{' '}
    {skiers.length} ski destinations, January highs in town range from {deg(Math.min(...skiers.map((d) => d.months[0].high)))} to
    {deg(Math.max(...skiers.map((d) => d.months[0].high)))}.
  </p>
</Guide>

<style>
  .ski th,
  .ski td {
    padding: 8px 6px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .ski th[scope='row'],
  .ski th[scope='rowgroup'] {
    text-align: left;
  }
  .ski .badge {
    padding: 2px 6px;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
  }
  .group th {
    background: var(--surface-2);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  th[scope='row'] a {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
